{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 jl_import_aaf\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Imports an AAF file into the current project: tracks, clips at the AAF's own timecode, embedded or linked audio, fades and crossfades, clip and track gain, pan, and volume and pan automation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pure Lua; nothing else to install. Tested on Windows with REAPER 7.73, with AAFs from Pro Tools 25.12 and Premiere Pro 26.2.2.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 reascripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER scripts by Jon Lloyd ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lloyd.work"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
lloyd.work
}}}
), distributed through ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER, choose {\i Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories...} and paste:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/jtllo/reascripts/raw/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Then use {\i Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages} to install the scripts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Script | Category | What it does | | --- | --- | --- | | {\f1 jl_import_aaf.lua} | Importers | Imports an AAF into the current project: tracks, clips at the AAF's own timecode, embedded or linked audio, fades and crossfades, clip and track gain, pan, and volume and pan automation. Pure Lua; nothing else to install. Tested on Windows with REAPER 7.73, with AAFs from Pro Tools 25.12 and Premiere Pro 26.2.2. |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIT; see {\f1 LICENSE}.\par}
}
